1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:20,000
(Music playing)
 
(Music playing)

2
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Dem baş temaşevanên me yên hêja.
 
Good time, our dear viewers.

3
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Bi navê ekîba Ax û Welat...
 
In the name of the team of Ax û Welat (Land and Country)...

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
em bernameya Ax û Welat li we pîroz dikin.
 
we congratulate you on the Ax û Welat program.

5
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Di salên dirêj de em ê di nav miletê me bigerin,
 
Through the long years we will travel among our people,

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
gund bi gund, bajar bi bajar, welat bi welat,
 
village by village, city by city, country by country,

7
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
çanda Kurda, çanda Ereba, çanda Xiristiyanan...
 
the culture of Kurds, the culture of Arabs, the culture of
Christians...

8
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
em ê bînin ser ekrana Ronahî TV.
 
we will bring it to the screen of Ronahî TV.

9
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Temaşevanên me yên hêja...
 
Our dear viewers...

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
car din em li herêma Efrînê, li navçeya Mabeta.
 
once again we are in the Afrin region, in the Mabeta
district.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Em ê gundekî din ji navçeya Mabeta nas bikin,
 
We will get to know another village of the Mabeta district,

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
vê carê em ê biçin gundê Sêmalka.
 
this time we will go to Sêmalka village.

13
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Gelo ev nav ji ku hatiye,
 
I wonder where this name comes from,

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,000
em ê derbasî vî gundî bibin, em ê kîjan urf û adetên vî
gundî nas bikin,
 
we will enter this village, which of this village's customs
and traditions we will get to know,

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
malbatên têde jiyan dikin em ê nas bikin.
 
we will get to know the families living in it.

16
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Ev gund jî nêzîkî Çiyayê Hawarê ye,
 
This village is also close to Hawar Mountain,

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:13,000
em jî bi hev re vê dema xweş bi hev re derbas bikin.
 
let's spend this good time together.

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:33,000
De ka em bi hev re gundê Sêmalka nas bikin.
 
Come on, let's get to know Sêmalka village together.

19
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Belê, îro jî em neha di nav zeytûnan de ne,
 
Yes, today we are currently among the olive trees,

20
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,000
em li gundê Sêmalka ne.
 
we are in Sêmalka village.

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Ka em binêrin ev jin li vir zeytûnan ji darê radikin.
 
Let's see these women here picking olives from the tree.

22
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Dema sala zeytûnan e,
 
It is the season of olives,

23
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
qewet be jinno.
 
more power to you, ladies.

24
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

25
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Em te nas bikin.
 
Let's get to know you.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome...

27
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Let's get to know you?

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Tu bi xêr hatî welatê xwe.
 
Welcome to your country.

29
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Saet xweş, em te nas bikin?
 
Thank you, let's get to know you?

30
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Navê min Elî ye ye, Elî ye Hesen, min ra dibên.
 
My name is Aliye, Aliye Hesen, they call me.

31
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Tu ji gundê Sêmalka yî?
 
Are you from Sêmalka village?

32
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Ez ji gundê Sêmalka me, em hatine alîkariya hevdû dikin.
 
I am from Sêmalka village, we came to help each other.

33
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Em bi vî rengî, em darên zeytûnan dadikişînin.
 
In this way, we pull down the olive trees.

34
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Tu Elî ye yî, te digot qey tu ji Mabeta bûyî.
 
You are Aliye, you used to say you were from Mabeta.

35
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Na ez ji gundê Sêmalka me, na!
 
No, I am from Sêmalka village, no!

36
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Ser çavê min.
 
Upon my eyes.

37
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Ka ez herim bal vê xwuşkê cem te jî.
 
Let me go to this sister next to you too.

38
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

39
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

40
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Çawa yî?
 
How are you?

41
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Te ji min dirêjtir bû ye ha.
 
Good, thank God.

42
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Te ji min dirêjtir bû ye ha.
 
You were taller than me.

43
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Ser silmê ye.
 
Standing on a bucket.

44
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Ha li ser silmê ye? Min go belkî ew qasî dirêj bûne.
 
Oh on a bucket? I said maybe they got that tall.

45
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Na na!
 
No no!

46
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Let's get to know you?

47
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Ehmediye Enter.
 
Ehmediye Enter.

48
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Ser çavê min.
 
Upon my eyes.

49
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

50
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Tu ji gundê Sêmalka yî?
 
Are you from Sêmalka village?

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

52
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Tu çend sal in, tu têyî nav darên, têyî nav zeytûnan?
 
How many years have you been coming among the trees, coming
among the olives?

53
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Wile ji zarotiya xwe ve, emrê min e.
 
By God, since my childhood, it's my life.

54
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Emrê te çiqas e? Xwedê emrekî xweş bide te.
 
How old are you? May God give you a good life.

55
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Ehlen we sehlen, şêst û yek sal e.
 
Welcome, sixty-one years.

56
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Şêst û yek.
 
Sixty-one.

57
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Te çû dibistanê?
 
Did you go to school?

58
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

59
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Te mekteb çend xwendiye?
 
What grade did you study up to?

60
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Heta duda.
 
Up to second.

61
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Te di nîvî de xera kirî?
 
You ruined it halfway?

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Min xera kir, erê wile.
 
I ruined it, yes by God.

63
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Qewet be jinno, qewet be.
 
More power to you ladies, more power to you.

64
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Merheba ji te re jî, em te jî nas bikin.
 
Hello to you too, let's get to know you too.

65
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Selam, navê min Ehmed e.
 
Peace, my name is Ehmed.

66
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes.

67
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Çavên te sax bin. Ehmedê Şêxo, Sêmalka me.
 
May your eyes be healthy. Ehmed of Şêxo, I am from Sêmalka.

68
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Ser çavê min. Çavên te sax bin.
 
Upon my eyes. May your eyes be healthy.

69
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,000
Zeytûnên kê ne ev?
 
Whose olives are these?

70
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Ev zeytûn ên Ebû Nîdal in.
 
These olives belong to Abu Nidal.

71
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Reşad...
 
Reshad...

72
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Reşad, Ebû Nîdal, ji gund e. Cîranê me ye.
 
Reshad, Abu Nidal, he's from the village. He's our neighbor.

73
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Hûn bi hevra hatin û bi alîkariyê.
 
You came together and to help.

74
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Em hevdu re alîkariyê dikin, em kîsên xwe radikin. Mûsim e.
 
We help each other, we pick up our bags. It's the season.

75
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Û ew jî tê ba we?
 
And does he come to you too?

76
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Wile ê me hene, ew tê nebin.
 
By God we have ours, he comes if we don't.

77
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Tê tine bin.
 
You have none.

78
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Erê wellehî îsal, ne sal a xwu ye.
 
Yes by God, this year, it's not its year.

79
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Na sala xwu ye na sala xwu be, tê tine bin îsal.
 
Whether it's its year or not, you have none this year.

80
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Hm...
 
Hm...

81
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Qewet be jinno.
 
More power to you ladies.

82
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Ka em hinekî bipirsin cem jinên din jî,
 
Let's ask some other women too,

83
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
ka ev jina cem te destpêkê beriya em diçin cem jina din...
 
let's see this woman next to you first before we go to the
other woman...

84
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome...

85
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Saet xweş. Em kêfa xwu jê re tînin ji te nas dikin.
 
Thank you. We enjoy getting to know you.

86
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Navê min Elî ye ye, mir ra dibêjin Ebû Egîd...
 
My name is Aliye, they call me Abu Egid...

87
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Tu pîra Egîd e?
 
You are Egid's grandmother?

88
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

89
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Ser serî min, ser çavên min.
 
Upon my head, upon my eyes.

90
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Xalo pîrê Elî, naha çiqas darê zeytûna heye l'vê Sêmalka?
 
Uncle, grandmother Aliye, how many olive trees are there now
in this Sêmalka?

91
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Teqrîben ango bi vî gundî me da hesibandin hesaba gundê me
dorî teqrîben dorî şêst hezar dar, gerek zeytûnê hebin.
 
Approximately, meaning in our village, we calculated the
account of our village around, approximately around sixty
thousand trees, olives should be there.

92
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Şêst hezar darên zeytûnê.
 
Sixty thousand olive trees.

93
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Gerek di gundê me da hebin.
 
Should be in our village.

94
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Ê sînorên gund li ku derê ne ango erdê wê.
 
And where are the borders of the village, meaning its land?

95
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Texmîna di sînorên me, digihîje nêzîkî gundê Şorbe.
 
Guessing within our borders, it reaches close to Şorbe
village.

96
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Ji alî gundê Şorbe, ji alî rojavê da, digihîje gundê Şorbe,
ji vî alî rojavê da digihîje Xwîtka.
 
From the side of Şorbe village, from the west side, it
reaches Şorbe village, from this west side it reaches
Xwîtka.

97
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Digihîje Rêka Ziftê.
 
It reaches the Asphalt Road.

98
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Ji vî alî da jî digihîje teqrîben...
 
From this side too it reaches approximately...

99
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
...gelî... em dibêjin gelî Ziravkê.
 
...valley... we say Ziravk valley.

100
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Gelî Ziravkê?
 
Ziravk valley?

101
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Ji vir da jî digihîje geliyê Ziravkê. Teqrîben yanî dor
berên me iştewane ev milkiyên me ne û em bi hev re hal
dikin.
 
From here too it reaches Ziravk valley. Approximately, I
mean our surroundings are like this, these are our
properties and we manage them together.

102
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Vî milkiyê we jî çiyayê Hawarê ye.
 
This property of yours is also Hawar mountain.

103
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Vî alî jî kurba jî, em vê ra dibêjin çiyayê Hawarê milkên
me, wî da jî dare...
 
This side too, nearby, we call it Hawar mountain, our
properties, over there too are trees...

104
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Û em hatin em bi hevdû ra alîkar dikin.
 
And we came, we help each other.

105
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Em ji vî yanî em dibêjin, beriya zivistan baran were,
 
We from this, I mean we say, before winter and rain comes,

106
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,000
em em karê xwe, em zû xelas bikin
 
we finish our work quickly,

107
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
em têde, bi hev re, em bi vî rengî têda dişixulin.
 
we work in it together, in this way we work in it.

108
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Naha heyamek kengî hûn ê biçin ji zeytûnê din re?
 
Now what time will you go to other olives?

109
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Teqrîben yanî heta sal yanî zeytûn kêmane,
 
Approximately, I mean until a year, I mean olives are less,

110
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:13,000
sêrek in hene. Teqrîben bi me re dimîne dorî bîst rojan bîst
û pênc rojan, ê dirêj bike wisa.
 
there are sparse ones. It will stay with us for about twenty
days, twenty-five days, it will last like that.

111
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Yanî ha niha hûn meha yazdehan, hûn meha dehan yekê de ne
ha?
 
I mean, oh now you are in the eleventh month, you are on the
first of the tenth month?

112
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Em di meha dehan, yekê de ne, yanî bi xêr û xweşî em heta
dehan û pêncê meha yanzdehan.
 
We are on the first of the tenth month, I mean with goodness
and health we will continue until the tenth and fifteenth of
the eleventh month.

113
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Yanî înşela teqrîben em ê xelas bikin, heke sal, sal ji me
ra, zeytûn kêmane.
 
I mean God willing approximately we will finish, if the
year, the year for us, olives are less.

114
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Bi vî rengî em karên xwu, em zû xelas bikin, em ê zeytûnên
xwe xelas bikin.
 
In this way our works, we finish quickly, we will finish our
olives.

115
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Neha gund piranî ha... zeytûn e?
 
Now the village is mostly... olives?

116
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Hemî, piranî zeytûn e. Zeytûn.
 
All, mostly it's olives. Olives.

117
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Lê ya li pey zeytûna çi te?
 
But what comes after olives?

118
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Li pey zeytûna teqrîben, ji me ceme ard jî hinek hene, arda
me jî hinek e,
 
After olives approximately, we have some lands too, our land
is also a bit,

119
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:45,000
em jî carna yanî qismekî arda jî wira da, kêm teqrîben
hindek garis lê diki...
 
we also sometimes I mean a part of the land over there, less
approximately some wheat is planted in it...

120
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:53,000
em gundê xwu heta em bidar kin û hawayê, em... weke ez
bêjime ceme... piraniya wî zeytûn in yanî. Tiştekî dî de
tinne yanî.
 
we to sustain our village and weather, we... like I say for
us... most of it is olives, I mean. There's nothing else in
it, I mean.

121
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Meqser jî hene li gund?
 
Are there also olive presses in the village?

122
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Meqsebe jî li gund hene...
 
Olive presses are also in the village...

123
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Ê, zeytûnê we jî hene, hûn ... Zeyta darxicê hene, ev weqas
di gund de...?
 
And, you have your olives too, you ... Are there olive oil
extractors, this much in the village...?

124
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Erê hene meqse jî hene em ê niha wêna kom bikin.
 
Yes there are presses too, we will collect them now.

125
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Em ê deynin tiraktoran, em ê... em ê çêdikin di tiraktorê
da, û dibin meqseba û dikin zeyt, ê zeytê xwe,
 
We will put them on tractors, we will... we will put them in
the tractor, and take them to the presses and make oil, make
our oil,

126
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,000
ev ki, ev ki difiroşe, kî mûna xwe datîne. Bi vî rengî, em
wî halî diborînin.
 
this one, this one sells, whoever keeps their provision. In
this way, we pass that condition.

127
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Qewet be jinno.
 
More power to you ladies.

128
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Ez biçim cem dayika jî... spas ji te re jî dikim.
 
Let me go to the mother too... thank you too.

129
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Saet xweş be... Qewet be jinno... Merheba jinno...
 
Thank you... More power to you ladies... Hello ladies...

130
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Welcome...

131
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Let's get to know you?

132
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Fadîle.
 
Fadile.

133
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Sêmalko Fadîle?
 
Fadile from Semalka?

134
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

135
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Em ka te jî nas bikin? Navê te bikim.
 
Let's get to know you too? Let me mention your name.

136
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Navê min Henîfe ye.
 
My name is Henife.

137
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Serserê min... Tu ji kîjan gundî yî?
 
Upon my head... Which village are you from?

138
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Sêmalka bi xwe me, ez ne kaniyo ne, Sêmalko me.
 
I am from Sêmalka itself, I am not a spring, I am Sêmalko.

139
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Û berê?
 
And before?

140
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Ji Elandarê me.
 
I am from Elandar.

141
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Ooo, Elandarê?
 
Ooo, Elandar?

142
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Ji navçeya Reco ye? Ji herêma Reco.
 
Yes.

143
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Ji navçeya Reco ye? Ji herêma Reco.
 
Is it from Rajo district? From Rajo region.

144
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

145
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Tu vira da çawa yî li vir bûyî?
 
How have you been here, you became from here?

146
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Bûka vira me.
 
I am the bride of here.

147
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Ser çavê min dayê.
 
Upon my eyes mother.

148
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Serê te sax be.
 
May your head be healthy.

149
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Dayê te anîn zeytûna.
 
Mother, they brought you to the olives.

150
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Em yarmediya hevdû dikin.
 
We are helping each other.

151
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Bûk...
 
Bride...

152
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Ne, wek din dixebitin.
 
No, working like this.

153
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Dayê hûn saet çenda derdikevin ji mal, diçin zeytûna?
 
Mother, what time do you leave home, go to the olives?

154
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Em saet şeş û nîva, teynin şeş nîv û, teynin.. em radibin...
 
We at six thirty, they bring at six thirty, they bring.. we
get up...

155
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Şeşan...
 
At six...

156
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Şeş û nîva, radibin.
 
At six thirty, we get up.

157
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Hûn taştê li mal dixwin an li vir dixwin?
 
Do you eat breakfast at home or eat here?

158
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Saet deh û dudu taştê dixwin...
 
Lih...

159
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Saet deh û dudu taştê dixwin...
 
And?

160
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Saet deh û dudu taştê dixwin...
 
At ten and two we eat breakfast...

161
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Çayên xwe vedixwin?
 
Drink your tea?

162
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Çayê xwe vedixwin, qehwê vedixwin, nanê xwe dixwin.
 
Drink our tea, drink coffee, eat our bread.

163
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Hûn karê xwe jî dikin.
 
You also do your work.

164
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Em karê xwu jî dikin. Pêş da kar wisa ye... tiştek nayê...
 
We do our work too. Because work is like this... nothing
comes...

165
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Naha tu çend salî yî, zeytûna ra radikî?
 
Now how old are you, picking olives?

166
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Wile, ez gori, ez labata zanim, na.
 
By God, I swear, I don't know much, no.

167
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Tu d'teniyê xwu...
 
You in your loneliness...

168
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Ez xwu ji çil salî, ji çil salî pêştir em tînin...
 
I for forty years, for more than forty years we have been
bringing...

169
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Erê...
 
Are you just a villager?

170
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Erê...
 
Yes...

171
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Naha, yekê zêde bikim... ez ê bikim.
 
Now, let me add one more... I will do it.

172
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Emrê te çiqas e?
 
To whom?

173
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,000
Emrê te çiqas e?
 
How old are you?

174
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Welle ez ne qena şêst heye, nizam çine...
 
By God, I don't know, maybe sixty, I don't know what...

175
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Maşelle. Xwedê sehhet û xweş bide.
 
Mashallah. May God give you health and goodness.

176
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Bide te jî.
 
May He give you too.

177
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Emrê xweş bide te.
 
May He give you a good life.

178
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Bide te jî.
 
May He give you too.

179
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Û... naha... zeytûna... kî berhev dike... jin ava dikin mêr
ava nakin?
 
And... now... olives... who collects them... women do it,
men don't do it?

180
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Çima? Em berhev dikin, ew jî hildişînin j'darê.
 
Why? We collect them, they also shake them from the tree.

181
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Hinek berhev dikin, hinek daweşînin...
 
Some collect, some shake down...

182
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Hinek didin ser silmê ne, hinek jor e...
 
Some put them on the bucket, some are up...

183
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Belê. Yekîk derdora wan da, yê din...
 
Yes.

184
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Belê. Yekîk derdora wan da, yê din...
 
Yes. One is around them, the other...

185
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Ez çawa alkariyê bikim ez jî amade me?
 
How can I help, I am ready too?

186
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Ez nevîm ez nizam çawa dibêjim.
 
I don't want to, I don't know how to say it.

187
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Ez nevêjim e xwu!
 
I am not throwing myself!

188
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Êdî te hawa, te hawa, ew bî...
 
Now you this way, you this way, let it be...

189
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Ez hawa me?
 
Am I this way?

190
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Ez kanim?
 
Can I?

191
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Merheba!
 
Yes I know.

192
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Merheba!
 
Hello!

193
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Qewet be ji te ra.
 
More power to you.

194
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
Qewet be ji te re jî xorto.
 
More power to you too, young man.

195
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Navê te bi xêr?
 
Your name please?

196
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Navê min Mistefa ye.
 
My name is Mistefa.

197
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Mistefa tu gundî yî ku yî?
 
Mistefa, which village are you from?

198
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Sêmalko me.
 
I am from Sêmalko.

199
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Tu gundê Sêmalka ne?
 
Are you from Sêmalka village?

200
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Li...
 
L...

201
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Yek ji gemarîkî têne ne li cem ve?
 
One from dirtiness doesn't come near you?

202
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Na, kes ji gemarîkî tê nîne, em kê Sêmalko ne.
 
No, no one from dirtiness comes, we are from Sêmalko.

203
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Qewet be ji te re.
 
More power to you.

204
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Ez xerîbê welatê me.
 
I am a stranger to my country.

205
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Gul û bînê çavên we me.
 
I am the rose and sight of your eyes.

206
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
Ez xerîbê welatê me.
 
I am a stranger to my country.

207
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Gul û bînê çavên we me.
 
I am the rose and sight of your eyes.

208
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Gula sor û çilmisî ya me.
 
The red and faded rose for us.

209
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Dûrketime ji xwudîya me.
 
I fell far away from our master.

210
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Ez xerîbê welatê me.
 
I am a stranger to my country.

211
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Ez xerîbê welatê me.
 
I am a stranger to my country.

212
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Min...
 
I...

213
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Êrê, keriyê nanê sêlê ye.
 
Oh, the piece of flatbread.

214
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Firavîna li ber palê ye.
 
Lunch by the side of the field.

215
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Min bîr kiriye nanê sêlê ye.
 
I missed the flatbread.

216
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Firavîna li ber palê ye.
 
Lunch by the side of the field.

217
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Şevbêrka me derbas dibû,
 
Our evenings used to pass,

218
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Bi çîroka û pîroka lê.
 
With tales and stories.

219
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Şevbêrka me derbas dibû,
 
Our evenings used to pass,

220
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Bi çîroka û pîroka lê.
 
With tales and stories.

221
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Ez xerîb im, welatê me ye.
 
I am a stranger in our homeland.

222
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Ez xerîb im, welatê me ye.
 
I am a stranger in our homeland.

223
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Ez xerîb im, welatê me ye.
 
I am a stranger in our homeland.

224
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Gelo bîna çavê we me.
 
I wonder if I am the light of your eyes.

225
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Gula sor im, çilmisî me.
 
I am a red rose, I am withered.

226
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Dûr ketiye ji xwediyê me.
 
It has fallen far from its owner.

227
00:10:49,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Ez xerîb im, welatê me ye.
 
I am a stranger in our homeland.

228
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, bi rastî jî cihek herî xweş dîmena
welatê me Rojava ye.
 
Yes, dear viewers, truly one of the most beautiful places is
the scenery of our homeland Rojava.

229
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Li çolê ye.
 
It is in the countryside.

230
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Kuder e?
 
Where is it?

231
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Di çolê ye.
 
It is in the countryside.

232
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Ev gund kuder e?
 
Where is this village?

233
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Ev gundê Sêmalka ye.
 
This is Semalka village.

234
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Ka em ber bi milê vir ve herin, ka em jinan wextê çawa
bixebitin. Em sekin...
 
Let's head this way, let's see how the women work. Let's
stand...

235
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Rojbaş, rojbaş jinên baş!
 
Good morning, good morning, good women!

236
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Merheba ji we re!
 
Hello to you!

237
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Merhaba. Ser çavan.
 
Hello. Welcome.

238
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Ser çavê min dayê. Em we nas bikin.
 
Thank you, mother. Let's get to know you.

239
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Em te nas bikin dayê?
 
Can we get to know you, mother?

240
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Fehîme.
 
Fehime.

241
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Ser çavê min. Em te jî nas bikin?
 
Very well. Can we get to know you too?

242
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Zeyneb.
 
Zeyneb.

243
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Ser çavê min dayê.
 
Very well, mother.

244
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Dayê, berî we darê xilas kirin hûn tînin berhev dikin, na?
 
Mother, before you finish with the tree, you gather them,
right?

245
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Em berhev dikin carekî.
 
We gather them at once.

246
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Em tên, pêşî em poşetê xwe raxînin, darên xwe diweşînin.
 
We come, first we lay out our bags, and we shake the trees.

247
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Û poşetê tînin berhev dikin.
 
And we bring the bags and gather them.

248
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Û em sibehî saet şeşan tên, û êvarî wekî te dîtî em saet
çaran derdikevin.
 
And we come at six in the morning, and in the evening, as
you saw, we leave at four.

249
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Xwedê hevalê we be.
 
May God be with you.

250
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Dayê wekî jin hûn saet şeşan tên na?
 
Mother, as women, you come at six, right?

251
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Lê hûn wexta saet çendê ji xew şiyar dibin?
 
At six o'clock.

252
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Lê hûn wexta saet çendê ji xew şiyar dibin?
 
But what time do you wake up from sleep?

253
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Em bi xwedê zû em şiyar dibin yadê.
 
By God, we wake up early, my dear.

254
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Hûn xwarina xwe jî çêdikin berî hûn tên?
 
Do you also make your food before you come?

255
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Xwarina xwe, şîva xwe, çayê, nanê, fitara sibê em tînin, û
nîvro jî dibin...
 
Our food, our dinner, tea, bread, we bring our morning
breakfast, and lunch too...

256
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
Yanî hûn taştê hazir dikin û hûn tên li vir darê dixwin?
 
So you prepare breakfast and you come and eat it here by the
trees?

257
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Em hazir dikin, em tên li vir darê dixwin.
 
We prepare it, we come and eat it here by the trees.

258
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Yanî jin zûtir radibe. Heta mêr radibe tu xwarinê wî
çêdikî...
 
So the woman wakes up earlier. Until the man wakes up, you
make his food...

259
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Jin! Keda wê zor e, keko.
 
Women! Their labor is hard, brother.

260
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Ji çaxê rabê... ta çêkirina xwarinê wî bike, bişo, malê
bişo, kincan paqij ke, makîne bixebitîne.
 
From the moment she wakes up... until she makes his food,
washes, washes the house, cleans the clothes, runs the
machine.

261
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Dertên derve... tê nava zeytûna heta saet dehan, deh û
nîvan, yazdehan... nîvro nanê xwe dixwin.
 
They go out... she comes into the olives until ten, half
past ten, eleven... at noon they eat their bread.

262
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Yanî cefayê herî pir ê jinan e?
 
So the biggest suffering belongs to the women?

263
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Belê. Ê jinan e weleh.
 
Yes. It belongs to the women, by God.

264
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Mêrên me, hukmê xwe jî dikin.
 
Our husbands rule over us too.

265
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Lê, dibêjin zû bin, lez ke, bilezînin yalla em herin!
 
Because they say, be quick, hurry, hurry up, let's go!

266
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Belê zîrek in, yanî divê hûn bilezînin biçin nav zeytûna na?
 
Yes, they are clever, meaning you have to hurry up and go
into the olives, right?

267
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Lê, em zû da herin nav zeytûnan.
 
Yes, we go early into the olives.

268
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Mêr dema berî we dertên diçin mehsere, hûn ji bo malê karekî
din dikin?
 
When the men leave before you and go to the olive press, do
you do other work for the house?

269
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Lê.. kuro weleh mêr dertên mehsere, jin jî karê malê dikin..
 
Yes... boy, by God the men go to the olive press, and the
women do the housework..

270
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Dayê van zeytûnan hûn dikin çi tûn?
 
Mother, what do you do with these olives?

271
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Em wî van dikin..
 
We do this with them..

272
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Ev yê bin dara û ê ser dara ji hev qut dikin.
 
We separate the ones on the ground and the ones on the tree.

273
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Ev yê bin darê xirab e, ev ê ser darê jê baştir e.
 
The ones on the ground are bad, the ones on the tree are
better.

274
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Yê bin dara tama axê jê tê, yê ser dara tama axê jê nayê.
 
The ones on the ground taste like dirt, the ones on the tree
don't taste like dirt.

275
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Em ê ker kin û xoyê lê kin û em ê çêkin...
 
We will cut them and put salt on them and we will prepare
them...

276
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Paşê em pê lîmona tişta çêdikin.
 
Then we prepare them with lemon and things.

277
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Niha piştî we çinî ji malê, hûn van çawa hiltînin?
 
Now after you picked them for the house, how do you preserve
them?

278
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Lê, em vana hiltînin, em zeytûnan dişelînin.
 
Yes, we preserve them, we peel the olives.

279
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Û em vana dikelînin, ev êdî başqe ye ev in ku dighirsin.
 
And we boil them, this is different now, these are the ones
that turn into paste.

280
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Em dikin derman. Em vana çêdikin terîqeyek din, hûn dizanin,
em dandikan jê derdixin.
 
We use them as medicine. We make them in another way, you
know, we take the seeds out of them.

281
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Yanî wek makdûs, em devkî makdûs jê çêdikin.
 
I mean like makdous, we make oral makdous out of it.

282
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Dayê piştî hûn diçin mal, hûn çi karî dikin êvarî?
 
Mother, after you go home, what work do you do in the
evening?

283
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Em diçin şîvê dikin. Em diçin weke derê malê, derdora wî em
paqij bikin..
 
We go and make dinner. We go and clean the door of the
house, its surroundings..

284
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Kincên xwe dişon.
 
You wash your clothes.

285
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Lê em kincên xwe dişon, kincê qirêj em pê paqijiyek bikin.
 
Yes, we wash our clothes, we clean up the dirty clothes.

286
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Cîhek gîha, yek nav cil û berga... na meş e..
 
A grassy place, someone in their clothes... it doesn't
work..

287
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Yanî jinên sibehê dest pê dikin saet şeşan ta şevê radibin..
 
So the women start in the morning at six until the evening
when they sleep..

288
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Û derdikevin derve û ew diçin malê jî dixebitin?
 
And they go outside and they go home and work too?

289
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Lê.. mal jî dixebitin.
 
Yes.. they work at home too.

290
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Û mêrekî derket radibe diweste, dibe pîrek e vaye.
 
And a man goes out, gets up and stops, saying here is a
woman.

291
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Û em mêrivan îdare dikin.. kî zane, nizanin mêr karî idare
kin.
 
And we manage the men.. who knows, they don't know how men
can manage.

292
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Lê, em ku çûn mal... qet biçûk nîne, şîva xwe dikin, kincan
dişon û firaqên xwa bişon..
 
But, when we go home... it is not small at all, they make
their dinner, wash the clothes and wash their dishes..

293
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Qewet be jaro.
 
May you have strength, dear.

294
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Serçavan serxêrê be.
 
You are welcome, may it be good.

295
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Ez kêfxweş bûm bi nasîna te.
 
I was happy to meet you.

296
00:14:43,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Xwedê te jî xweş bike inşellah.
 
May God make you happy too, God willing.

297
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Gundê Sêmalka, girêdayî navçeya Mabeta ya kantona Efrînê, 14
kîlometre dûrî bajarokê Mabeta dikeve.
 
Semalka village, connected to the Mabeta district of Afrin
canton, is located 14 kilometers away from the town of
Mabeta.

298
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Ji ber ku gund di destpêkê de ji sê malbatan ava bû, lewra
ev nav lê hatiye kirin.
 
Because the village was originally built by three families,
this name was given to it.

299
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Ew jî malbata Çamo, Xado û Ringo bûn.
 
And they were the families of Chamo, Khado and Ringo.

300
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Van her sê malbatan gund şên kirin.
 
These three families built up the village.

301
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Lê piştre gelek eşîrên derdorê hatin û li gund niştecih bûn.
 
But later, many surrounding tribes came and settled in the
village.

302
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Di heyama şerê cîhanê yê yekemîn de, hemû mêrên malbata Çamo
di nava leşkerê osmanî de cih digirtin, û tev li wî şerî
bibûn.
 
During the First World War, all the men of the Chamo family
took their place in the Ottoman army, and participated in
that war.

303
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Lê tu kes ji wan venegeriya, tenê jinên wan man.
 
But none of them returned, only their wives remained.

304
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Yek ji gundê Gemrûkê bi navê Os, ango Ezîz, bi jineke ji
malbata Çamo re dizewice, û li gund dimîne.
 
One from Gemruk village named Os, meaning Aziz, married a
woman from the Chamo family, and stayed in the village.

305
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Malbata Heso, ji gundê Şêx Kêlê hatin.
 
The Heso family came from Sheikh Kêlê village.

306
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Hamaçî ji gundê Gulîkan hatin, û li gundê Sêmalka niştecih
bûn.
 
Hamachi came from Gulikan village, and settled in Semalka
village.

307
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Keçikek ji malbata Çamo, çû zewicî di nav malbata Şamî de
rûniştin.
 
A girl from the Chamo family got married and lived with the
Shami family.

308
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Malbata Heno jî ji gundê Sicû yê girêdayî Ezazê hatin.
 
The Heno family also came from Siju village connected to
Azaz.

309
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Malbata Seydo jî ji gundê Çiyê hatin.
 
The Seydo family also came from Çiyê village.

310
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Xelîlê Sêyid ê Eşê jî ji gundê Xalta hat.
 
Khalil Seyid Eshe also came from Khalta village.

311
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:34,000
Gundî Gemrûkê piştî demeke hat gundê Sêmalka, û bi keçeke ji
malbata Çamo re dizewice, û li gund dimîne.
 
After a while, a Gemruk villager came to Semalka village,
and married a girl from the Chamo family, and stayed in the
village.

312
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Omer jî ji Şêrawa hat û li gundê Sêmalka ma.
 
Omer also came from Sherawa and stayed in Semalka village.

313
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja, em derbasî gundê Sêmalka bûn.
 
Yes dear viewers, we passed to Semalka village.

314
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Û îro jî zate em ê vî gundî nas bikin.
 
And today we will get to know this village.

315
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Em spasîya miletê gund dikin, miletê gund jî zate, tiştên di
derdorê amade ye..
 
We thank the people of the village, the people of the
village are inherently ready with things around..

316
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Lê gelek jî hene di dema zeytûna ye.
 
But there are many also since it is olive season.

317
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Pir kes çûne ser karê xwe.
 
Many people have gone to their work.

318
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Em wan jî silav dikin, em spasîya wan jî dikin ji ber ku de
çûn ser karê xwe, dest bi karên xwe kirin.
 
We greet them too, we also thank them because they went to
their work, started their work.

319
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Niha jî dîroka vî gundî em bi kesekî nas bikin. Apê Reşad û
Apê Ednan falan hene ku em dîroka gundê Sêmalka ji wan
bipirsin.
 
Now let's get to know the history of this village with
someone. There is Uncle Reshad and Uncle Ednan and so on, so
we can ask them about the history of Semalka village.

320
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Merhaba ji te re Apê Reşad.
 
Hello to you, Uncle Reshad.

321
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Merhaba, ehlen wa sehlen.
 
Hello, welcome.

322
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Sax bî. Apê Reşad, em di dîwanê we ne.
 
Stay well. Uncle Reshad, we are in your diwan.

323
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Ser seran û ser çavan...
 
You are most welcome...

324
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Sax bî. Em destpêkê dîroka gundê we tê nas bikin.
 
Stay well. First, let's get to know the history of your
village.

325
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Navê gund ji ku hatiye?
 
Where did the name of the village come from?

326
00:17:51,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Sêmalka... Sê malbat hatin vir. Ji eşîra fîtrat ko, pir
dirêj e. Sê malbat hatine...
 
Semalka... Three families came here. From a long time ago.
Three families came...

327
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Malbata mala Çamo, û a mala Xado û mala Mistê Ringo... yanî
Xidê Ringo.
 
The family of Chamo's house, and Khado's house, and Miste
Ringo's house... meaning Khide Ringo.

328
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Yanî navê gund ji van sê malbatan hatiye.
 
So the name of the village came from these three families.

329
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Ji wê sê malbatê na... wisa sê mal bûn, lewre kirin sê mal.
Sêmalka, Sêmalka kire.
 
From those three families... so they were three houses, so
they made it three houses. Semalka, they made it Semalka.

330
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Na, gundekî din jî heye ew jî navê wî Sêmalka ye.
 
But there is another village, its name is also Semalka.

331
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Sêmalka heye ew... hema Sêmalka ye. Ne Sêmalkeyî em Gemrûkê
ne.
 
There is Semalka that... is just Semalka. We are not
Semalki, we are Gemruki.

332
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Destpêkê sê malbat bûn?
 
In the beginning, there were three families?

333
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Sê malbat bûn. Demeke pir dirêj sê malbat man heta nav lê
kirin.. yanî ew gund çêkirin sê malbat rûniştin li vê derê.
 
There were three families. For a very long time three
families stayed until they named it... meaning they built
that village, three families settled here.

334
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Paşê di du re, malbat kom dibin di vir de têne û rûdinin.
 
Then afterwards, families gather, come here and sit.

335
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Na, Apê Reşad di navbera we de gundê we...
 
No, Uncle Reshad, among you, your village...

336
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:58,000
Dema Osmanî derbas bûye, dema rejîma Baas derbas bûye..
 
When the Ottomans passed, when the Baath regime passed..

337
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Na.. rejîma Baas wextê hatî nav lê kirine 'Sehal'.
 
No.. when the Baath regime came, they named it 'Sehal'.

338
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Wateya wê çiye?
 
What is its meaning?

339
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Bi erebî ye, sehal. Tiştekî bikişînî. Sîhale yan fîlan..
 
It is in Arabic, sehal. To pull something. Sihale or so on..

340
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Û dema osmaniyan derbasî vir bûn ewî navê gundê we de
guhertin, hûn navê gund çawa dibêjin?
 
And when the Ottomans passed here, did they change the name
of your village, how do you say the village name?

341
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Ew Sêmalka ma.
 
It remained Semalka.

342
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Heta Seferberlikê hat, herba alemiyê ya yekê.
 
Until the Mobilization (Seferberlik) came, the first world
war.

343
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Çamo du lawên wî hebûn, ê mezin Reşo bû..
 
Chamo had two sons, the older was Resho..

344
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Ê biçûk jî Eşo bû.
 
And the younger was Esho.

345
00:19:50,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Reşo lawikî wî hebû.. zewicîbû.. navê wî Lêwê bû.. wê wextê
dertên derve diçin seferberlikê.
 
Resho had a son.. he was married.. his name was Lewe.. at
that time they go out and go to the mobilization.

346
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Reşo dimire, Hasû dimire, navê wî Asû ye, Asû jî dimire, lo
ew e Asû qeçekî xwe jî dimire...
 
Reşo passes away, Hasû passes away, his name is Asû, Asû
also passes away. Asû, even his child passes away...

347
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Dawî li wê qut dibe, ewê Reşo qut dibe.
 
It ends there, Reşo's line ends.

348
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Asû... çavê min re, birakî Reşo sê lawê wî hene.
 
Asû... my dear, Reşo's brother has three sons.

349
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Me'mû ye, Fîlo ye, Reşîd e.
 
They are Me'mû, Fîlo, and Reşîd.

350
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Evana eskeriya Seferberlikê dest pê dike, heta herba alemî
ya yekê.
 
This starts with the mobilization for military service,
until the First World War.

351
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Fîlo bi Me'mû ve, diherin eskeriya wan... diçin eskeriyê...
 
Fîlo and Me'mû go to the military... they go to military
service.

352
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Diçin kû derê?
 
Where do they go?

353
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Eskeriya Osmaniyan.
 
To the Ottoman military.

354
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
Yanî diçin şer dikin?
 
So they go to fight?

355
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Diçin şer. Erê, diçin şer.
 
They go to fight. Yes, they go to war.

356
00:20:51,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Diçin... diçin nafetilin. Me'mû zewicî bû, qîzek xwe hebû.
Dû re qîz jî dimire...
 
They go... they go and never return. Me'mû was married, he
had a daughter. Later, the daughter also dies...

357
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Û ew qut dibe, nema li ba bavê dimînin.
 
And his line ends, there's no one left in the father's
house.

358
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Birayê wî yê biçûk Reşîd dimîne. Ew Asû... sê bira ne...
 
His younger brother Reşîd remains. That Asû... they are
three brothers...

359
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Diherin herbê, Reşîd dimîne. Reşîd jî dibin mîna kaxizkî xwe
bi dest xistiye an kaxilek hebû. Lê wê demê... diçe eskeriyê
wê salê... dibêje ewê derê diçe ... di biharê... xebere tê
diherin deka Reşîd...
 
They go to war, Reşîd remains. Reşîd is told he got some
papers or something like that. But at that time... he goes
to the military that year... they say he's going there... in
the spring... news comes, they go to Reşîd's place...

360
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Dimire, ew jî nexweş dikeve, dibêjin li wê derê ketiye.
nexweş ketiye... û welleh, milletekî wê derê diherin,
dibînin bûye textê... eşq bûye. Le devê wê derê dikin tînin
wê derê. Li devê çawa nexweş bû nizanin. Nexweşî çi navî
lêkin nizanin, nexweşiya dimire.
 
He passes away, he also fell ill, they say he fell ill over
there. He got sick... and well, some people go there and see
him lying on the ground... like a board. They bring him from
there. How he got sick, they don't know. They don't know
what to call the disease, he dies from the illness.

361
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Mala Çomo qut dibe. Ji mêran da qut dibe, qîz dimînin. Qîzek
Reşo... Asû jî mir... qîzke xwe jî dimirin.
 
The Çomo family line ends. The male line ends, only
daughters remain. A daughter of Reşo... Asû also died... and
his daughters die too.

362
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Milk bi jinan dimîne... bi qîzan dimîne...
 
The property is left to the women... it's left to the
daughters.

363
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Ji qîza Gulik û Çerê ye, tê li wê derê rûdinê. Qîza Reşo
ye... tê li wê derê... milk fireh e... Li ser milkê bi jinî
rûdinê... Hemec.
 
She is the daughter of Gulik and Çerê, she comes and settles
there. Reşo's daughter... comes there... the property is
large... She settles on the property with her husband...
Hemec.

364
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,000
Lê wê rûdinê.
 
And she settles there.

365
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Lawkî xwe dibêje Hemîd... ji Hemîd efendiyê xwe re hal û
mesel, mal û mesel dibêje... dihêle, diçe dibe mal... digel
da rûniştin.
 
She tells her son Hemîd... tells her gentleman Hemîd the
whole situation and the story... he leaves and establishes a
home... they settled there.

366
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Evane şikestin, hêsîr man. Bas...mala Azê dibêjin, em jî li
Tirkiye ne, em jî...başûr...Kurdistana bakur in.
 
These people were broken, left captive. Anyway... the Azê
family says, we are also in Turkey, we are also... south...
Northern Kurdistan.

367
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Apê, te di nav gundî de got çend malbat hene? Yan jî navê
van malbatan hûn dikarin ji me re bibêjin?
 
Uncle, you mentioned how many families are in the village?
Or can you tell us the names of these families?

368
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Navê malbatan... mala Çomo yek. Mala Xedo didu. Mala Mistê
Rengo sisê. Mala Azê çar.
 
The names of the families... Çomo family one. Xedo family
two. Mistê Rengo family three. Azê family four.

369
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Mala Hisê pênc. Mala Hemecê şeş. Mala Şêrewî heft. Mala Hilê
heşt.
 
Hisê family five. Hemec family six. Şêrewî family seven.
Hilê family eight.

370
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Mala Xelîl Seydî Eşê neh. Mala Enter deh. Mala Heno yanzdeh.
Mala Silêman Kocer donzdeh.
 
Xelîl Seydî Eşê family nine. Enter family ten. Heno family
eleven. Silêman Kocer family twelve.

371
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:47,000
Mala Reşkî... Reşê sêzdeh. Sêzdeh malbat di gundî me da
hene, welleh şerîf. Ev sêzdeh malbat li vî gundî ne. Eşîr
yek... têkiliyên nêzîk... têkiliyek taybet di nav me de
heye, xapxap tune.
 
Reşkî family... Reşê thirteen. There are thirteen families
in our village, by God. These thirteen families are in this
village. One tribe... close relations... we have a special
bond among us, there's no deception.

372
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Kîjan eşîr e?
 
Which tribe is it?

373
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Eşîra Amkan e. Em tabî eşîra Amkan in li vir e.
 
It's the Amkan tribe. We belong to the Amkan tribe here.

374
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Yanî ev girêdayî eşîra Amkan e?
 
So this is connected to the Amkan tribe?

375
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Em girêdayî wê ne...
 
We are connected to it...

376
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Te behsa Kocer jî kir, Kocer jî hene...
 
You also mentioned Kocer, are there Kocer people too?

377
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Kocer e... Kocer... Gocer wek mesele dibêjin...Kocer zêde
barkirî ye, ji ber ku bar dikin, navê wan Gocer in.
 
Kocer... Kocer... they call them Gocer for example... Kocer
means they are heavily loaded, because they pack up and
move, their name is Gocer.

378
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Nuha, di her gundekî de, berê oda mêvanan hebû.
 
Now, in every village, there used to be guest rooms.

379
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Oda Şêx Seydo li wê derê cem me hebû. Belkî dora çil salî jî
dirêj kir, çil salî muxtarê gund bû. Ew mêrekî însan bû... û
piştî wefata ku çêbû... qeçkan nekir.
 
We had Şêx Seydo's room there. It lasted for maybe forty
years, he was the village headman for forty years. He was a
good man... and after his passing... the children didn't
continue it.

380
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,000
Na berê... di gundî we de rihspiyê we kî bû?
 
No, before... who was the elder of your village?

381
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Rihspiyê me Şêx Seydo bû.
 
Our elder was Şêx Seydo.

382
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Hemîdê Hemecê bû. Mistê Heso bû, Xelîl Seydî Eşo bû, kurê
Hilê bû... Evana yanî rûspiyê gund bûn. Tiştek nîzahek biba,
çi dikirin... mabenî evan çareser dikirin.
 
It was Hemîd Hemec. Mistê Heso, Xelîl Seydî Eşo, Hilê's
son... These were the prominent figures of the village. If
there was any dispute, they would resolve it among
themselves.

383
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Gundê we çend xanî tê de hene?
 
How many houses are in your village?

384
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Gundê me, dor sed û deh xanî ne.
 
Our village has around a hundred and ten houses.

385
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:53,000
Sed û deh xanî di gund de hene... Tê tiştekî din bibêjî?
 
There are a hundred and ten houses in the village... Do you
have anything else to add?

386
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Saxiya te wexweş be.
 
Good health to you.

387
00:24:55,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Spasiya te dikim. Apê Reşad, gotina te heye? Tiştekî din
bibêjî ser gund?
 
Thank you. Uncle Reşad, do you have any words? Anything else
to say about the village?

388
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:04,000
Saxiya te xweş, ez spasiya we dikim.
 
Good health to you, I thank you.

389
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Mala we ava be.
 
May your house prosper.

390
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Ew jî ava be. Batinê can me... em pir şa bûn, xelkê me zêde
bernameyê we nas dikin. Gundi ev sê malên ko... kî û li kû
derê ye..
 
Yours as well. From the bottom of our hearts... we are very
happy, our people know your program well. The villagers of
these three families... who is where..

391
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:22,000
Yanî li ser bilindî ko ji we ra...
 
I mean on the high ground for you...

392
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Spasiya me jî... em jî pir kêfxweş bûn. Û me we nas kir.. em
derbasî gundê we bûn. Xwedê kêmasiya we nede. Em spasiya we
dikin. Dembaş.
 
Our thanks as well... we were also very happy. And we got to
know you... we visited your village. May God not let you
lack anything. We thank you. Have a good time.

393
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:07,000
Li bakurê gundê Zeviyê Zeytûna, bîra kevnareya riyaseriya
Efrîn û gundê Şêxo diket.
 
To the north of the village are olive fields, the ancient
well of the Afrin countryside, and the village of Şêxo.

394
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Li rojavayê zinarat keka seh bike. Çemê Ziravkê û Sêkanî
hene.
 
Look to the west at the rocky terrain. There are the Ziravkê
and Sêkanî rivers.

395
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Kaniya Qestelê, Çinarê û Çavreşkê. Herdu gundên Xirabê Rota
û Avrazê li bakur...
 
The Qestel, Çinar, and Çavreşk springs. The two villages of
Xirabê Rota and Avraz to the north...

396
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:27,000
Zeviyê zeytûnan, zinarat keka Qere Erselan û çiyayê Hawarê.
Li rojavayê zeviyên zeytûnan... Gola Avê û gundê Şorbe.
 
Olive fields, the rocky terrain of Qere Erselan, and the
Hawar mountain. To the west, olive fields... Gola Avê and
the village of Şorbe.

397
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:34,000
Xelkê gundê Sêmalika, debar û jiyana xwe bi çandiniyê
dikin... ji zeviyê zeytûnan, bexçe û rezan.
 
The people of Sêmalika village make a living through
agriculture... from olive fields, orchards, and vineyards.

398
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Nêzî deh kesî sewalkariyê dikin. Û derdorê bîst û pênc kes
di sazî û desteyên Rêveberiya Xweser li Mabetê û Efrînê
dixebitin.
 
About ten people practice animal husbandry. And around
twenty-five people work in the institutions and boards of
the Autonomous Administration in Mabeta and Afrin.

399
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Merheba anê.
 
Hello, mother.

400
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Çawa yî dayê, tu baş î? Tehet. (Saxlemî?) Baş î? Saxlem.
 
Welcome.

401
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Çawa yî dayê, tu baş î? Tehet. (Saxlemî?) Baş î? Saxlem.
 
How are you, mother, are you well? How is your health? Are
you well? Healthy?

402
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Can we know who you are?

403
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:37,000
Te nas kirim... Navê min Sewlê ye, û ev jî mala min e.
 
You know me... My name is Sewlê, and this is my home.

404
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,000
Ser çavan anê dayê.
 
Welcome, mother.

405
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Tu jî nas bike, merheba li we jinbirê, tu başî?
 
Introduce yourself too, hello sister-in-law, are you well?

406
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,000
Merheba li we jî.. Ehlen we sehlen...
 
Hello to you too.. Welcome...

407
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Navê te jinbirê?
 
What is your name, sister-in-law?

408
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Navê min Ferîde ye.
 
My name is Ferîde.

409
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:50,000
Ser çavan dayê. Te derman çêdikirin dayê? Em hatin cem te...
 
Welcome, mother. Were you making medicines, mother? We came
to see you...

410
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Derman welle dikim.
 
Yes, I make medicine by God.

411
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Tu çi çêdikî?
 
What do you make?

412
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Ji zarokê biçûk ku nexweş dibin. An jî ji nişka ve tiştek lê
tê, ez derman dikim.
 
For small children when they get sick. Or if something
suddenly happens to them, I treat them.

413
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Ev kar... çend sal in tu vî karî dikî?
 
This work... how many years have you been doing this work?

414
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Na ez nakim... ez pûç nakim... dema nexweş tê ez wele derman
dikim, ew baş dibe.
 
No, I don't... I don't fail... when a patient comes, by God,
I treat them, and they get better.

415
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,000
Yanî her kes tê cem te?
 
So everyone comes to you?

416
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Îcab dike nexweş tên, yên ku nexweş in tên, an na nayên.
 
When necessary, the sick come, those who are ill come,
otherwise they don't.

417
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Yanî ji zû de tu vî karî dikî ha?
 
So you've been doing this work for a long time, huh?

418
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Ji zû ve, belê.
 
For a long time, yes.

419
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Çend sal in?
 
How many years?

420
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:20,000
Hema dor bîst salan e. Wê çaxê nexweşiyan min re dida
nîşandan.
 
Almost around twenty years. At that time, illnesses would
show themselves to me.

421
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:24,000
Yanî te xwesî ya xwe dît.. te xwe fêr kir...
 
So you saw your mother-in-law.. you learned it yourself...

422
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Belê, xwesîya min min hîn kir, belê.
 
Yes, my mother-in-law taught me, yes.

423
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:28,000
Rehmetî ya xesîya te vî karî dikir?
 
Your late mother-in-law used to do this work?

424
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:34,000
Hinekî... ez li wê dinihêrîm wê çêdikir, mêrê wê çêdikir...
piştre min dest pê kir.
 
Somewhat... I would watch her make it, her husband made
it... then I started.

425
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:43,000
Bêhna wan teng dibû, aciz dibûn... min derman dida wan.
Kesên ku baş dibûn, li nav gel digotin.
 
They would get breathless, become uneasy... I would give
them medicine. Those who got well would talk about it among
the people.

426
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Na tu kîjan nexweşiyan nas dikî û tu dikarî derman bikî?
 
Now, which diseases do you recognize and can you treat?

427
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Êdî zarokên pitik ez fam dikim...
 
I can understand infant children...

428
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Yanî çi qas kes hatin cem te?
 
So how many people have come to you?

429
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Pir hatin.
 
Many came.

430
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Pir hatin? Gelek hatine?
 
Many came? A lot have come?

431
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Gelek pir hatin.
 
A great many came.

432
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Ji kû derê dihatin ba te?
 
Where did they come from to see you?

433
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Ji Efrînê, ji derdora Efrînê.. li herêma Efrînê hinek
digot... hema yek di bîhîse yek tiştine ne... li ser Tirkiyê
dihatin... ji Helebê dihatin, Şamê dihatin. Ji Reqa
dihatin... dihate kî yek dibîhîstiye dihatin.
 
From Afrin, from the surroundings of Afrin.. in the Afrin
region some would say... as soon as one hears something..
they came from Turkey... they came from Aleppo, they came
from Damascus. They came from Raqqa... whoever heard about
it would come.

434
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Ji derûdorê te yanî gişt dihatin cem te?
 
So from all around you, they came to you?

435
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Derdora me tev dihatin.
 
All of our surroundings came.

436
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Zarokên wan gişt baş dibûn?
 
Did all of their children get well?

437
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Heye ku baş dibin.. nexweşiyên zik hebûn bi wan re baş
dibûn... min ji wan re digot eger çênebû dihatin ez ji wan
re dîtin min... nexweşînên din bi wan derman dibûn...
 
It happens that they get well.. they had stomach illnesses
which got well with them... I told them if they didn't get
better they could come and I would check them... other
sicknesses were treated with those.

438
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:33,000
Zarokên te wan fêr nabin? Dermanan nakin?
 
Don't your children learn this? They don't make medicines?

439
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Naxêr ji Şamê dikirîn ez hîn bûm e. Tiştek din na derman.
 
No, they would buy it from Damascus, I have learned it. I
don't use any other medicine.

440
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Yanî niha hember dermanên xwezayî kes tune ye na? Yan jinên
gund derman dikin?
 
So now there's no one doing natural medicine? Or do the
women of the village make medicine?

441
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Naxêr kes nake.
 
No, no one does.

442
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Gund de kes nîne?
 
There's no one in the village?

443
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:52,000
Jina xalê min perzerê (zerikê) dikir lê ew niha mir.
 
My uncle's wife used to treat jaundice, but she has passed
away now.

444
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Derheq nexweşiyê de tu dikarî tiştekî din bibêjî?
 
Can you say anything else about the illnesses?

445
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Ev hîç... ew tiştên derman ez dizanim... ev hîç.
 
That's nothing... those medicine things I know... that's
nothing.

446
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,000
Ê siheta te xweş be, dê.
 
May you be in good health, mother.

447
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:04,000
A te jî xweş be, bi xêr hatin ser çavan lawê min.
 
May you be as well, welcome, you are dear to me, my son.

448
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:07,000
Vê carê tiştên te jî cebarî ye.
 
This time your items are for bone setting.

449
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Eh.
 
Yes.

450
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Tu bi xwe xwe ji kê fêr bûyî? Kê hînî te kir?
 
From whom did you learn? Who taught you?

451
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Bavo dîsa rehma xwedê li kalê me, ew kalê me fêr bibû wê...
 
Son, again may God have mercy on our grandfather, our
grandfather had learned it...

452
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Kalê min ji kalê min, û ez jî bavê xwe fêr bûm.
 
My grandfather learned from his grandfather, and I learned
from my father.

453
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Rehma xwedê li wan be! Te bi xêra wan wisa...
 
May God have mercy on them! You learned thanks to them like
this...

454
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Bavê min, dîsa sed car rehma Xwedê lê be, di dest bavê min
hîn bûm.
 
My father, again a hundred times may God have mercy on him,
I learned at my father's hands.

455
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Tu bi xwe li gundê Qotanê yî an... ?
 
Are you yourself from Qotanê village or...?

456
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Na bavo ez ne ji Şiyê me. Ez ji gundê Qotanê me.
 
No son, I'm not from Şiyê. I am from Qotanê village.

457
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Tu li gundê Qotanê yî?
 
You are in Qotanê village?

458
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

459
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Serçavê te, navê bavê te çi bû?
 
What was the name of your father?

460
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:31,000
Nesan.
 
Nesan.

461
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Nesan. Navê Nesan navdar bû, her kesî nas dikir?
 
Nesan. Was the name Nesan famous, did everyone know him?

462
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Lê belê di gund û mentîqan nas dikir.
 
Yes, they knew him in the village and the regions.

463
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Erê, welleh gelek cebarçî hene, ev nav belav bû dengên wan
hene.
 
Yes, by God, there are many bone setters, this name and
their reputation spread.

464
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Kemal heye, u Nebî Heskê, u Ebdî Heskê an hebû? Gelek
hene...
 
There is Kemal, and Nebi Heske, and Ebdi Heske, right? There
are many...

465
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Ew jî hebûn e, em çûçik bûn.
 
They existed too, we were very young.

466
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Yek şikestibû, an tiştek dî... yan yek milê wî derketibû,
milê diket am li ser disekinîn.
 
When someone broke a bone, or something else... or when
someone's shoulder got dislocated, we used to stand over
them.

467
00:30:54,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Min nêrî we u çêdikiri, min fêhm dikir, an u ez hîn dibû.
 
I watched him fixing it, I understood it, and I learned.

468
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Heta ez canek bûm u mezin bûm, min şerm dikir destê mêran u
jinan... eyb e min wisa nedikir.
 
Until I became a young woman and grew up, I was shy to touch
the hands of men and women... it was a shame, I didn't do
it.

469
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:10,000
Min hişt... şikestinek an jinek çêbû... wê şûnda min dest pê
kir.
 
I left it... then there was a fracture or a woman... after
that I started doing it.

470
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:12,000
Te bavê xwe bi vî rengî didît... an?
 
Did you see your father doing it in this way... or?

471
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Bavê min, milê yekî derketibû, we dî çêdikiri min ji wî fêr
kir u fêhm kir.
 
My father, someone's shoulder was dislocated, I watched him
fixing it and I learned and understood from him.

472
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Wî fêhm kir bavo wê em wê dest u şidand... an wî.
 
He understood son, we pressed the hand and tightened... and
that's it.

473
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Ez û mezin em şûnda man... wexta tiştek dişkest ez nav
çêdikirim.
 
We grew up and stayed... when something broke I used to fix
it.

474
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Di gund de... xelk diketin tu tiştek... cebar nedikir?
 
In the village... people fell, didn't you set any bones?

475
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Kalikê me çêdikirin... kalik me wisa an.
 
Our grandfathers used to do it... our grandfathers like
that.

476
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Paşiyê min dest bi vî karî kir u bavê min ez hîn bûm u min
dest pê kir.
 
Later I started doing this work, and from my father I
learned and I started doing it.

477
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Erê bavo, berê duxtor tunebû, u nexweşxane dûr bû, erebe
tunebû, milet birçî bû...
 
Yes my dear, in the past there were no doctors, and the
hospital was far, there were no cars, the people were
hungry...

478
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Milet u gundiyan xwe dispêrin van karan... cebarçî u ew
tiştan piranî di gundan de bûn.
 
People and villagers relied on these practices...
bonesetters and these things were mostly in the villages.

479
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Her tişt yan milê derketî an tiştek din bi wan tiştan...
tiştek çêdibû min datanî... dida pêş.
 
Everything, whether a dislocated shoulder or something
else... if something happened I used to put it... push it
back.

480
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Zarok jî u tê fêr... dihatin te zarok jî çêdikiri?
 
And children too... did they come, did you fix children as
well?

481
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Zarok yan kal bû ez... ez datanî wan min çêdikiri u fêr im.
 
Whether a child or an old person... I put them and fixed
them, I am skilled.

482
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:58,000
Te mil u tişt wî dişikestî bû, dest şikiya bû, te milî wî ew
min bi paçek...
 
Whether a shoulder and things broke, or a hand broke, the
shoulder I used to use a bandage...

483
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Pê derdiket, ez u wekî dar... dest bi wî dar me yê digirt...
me wê dikişand an... derdiket pê.
 
If it came out, I... like a stick... held the hand with a
stick... we pulled it... and it popped out.

484
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:10,000
Dayê me behs kir, te cebarçî... carna jinek li Şiyê cebarî
dikir an navdar... tu çawa wî qey hîn bû?
 
Mother, we talked about it, you as a bonesetter... sometimes
a famous woman in Shiye would do bone setting... how did you
get used to it?

485
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Min jî ez wan nizanibû... ez fêr bûm an min ez... ez tişt
fêr me ez dest pê kim we... wî.
 
I didn't know them... I learned it and I... I learned things
so I started doing it...

486
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Min tişt wê mezin me şerm e wisa ez wê fêhm kir...
 
It's a big thing for me, it's a shame, that's how I
understood it...

487
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Ez nedihiştim, u qebûl nedihişt bavê min u we ew ez te.
 
I didn't let it happen, and my father didn't accept it, and
that's how it was.

488
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Yanî ew tiştek e wek gelek zahmet te an... çawa te we
çêdikir te?
 
I mean, if it's something very difficult... how did you fix
it?

489
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Ew we tiştî hûr an wisa... jinek mezin ew an me wê çêdikir
wê hêsan dibû u wê wî... me wî...
 
It was something small or like that... an older woman, we
would fix it, it would become easy... we...

490
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:33,000
We xwar bi aliyekî... em pênc deqe we yê we tu me dikişand
tu dest min de.
 
If it was bent to one side... in five minutes we would pull
it while my hand was on it.

491
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Tiştek an zehmet tu bi dest nediket?
 
Did you ever encounter anything difficult that you couldn't
do?

492
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Çiqas şikestin be an we di wê de... u we me we ez we dest
datînim min fêr dibû... tu de me yê heta derdixist.
 
No matter how severe the fracture is... I used to put my
hand on it, I was skilled... until it came out.

493
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Min bihîst dîsa wî we jina li gund e... li Şiyê wê te nas
nedikir?
 
I heard again that there is a woman in the village... in
Shiye, didn't you know her?

494
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Wele we nav Ebdî Heskê, nav wî wisa me cebarçî jin bûn... u
wî u.
 
By God, the name of Ebdi Heske, that's the name of female
bonesetters... and them.

495
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:56,000
Ew me dît, jin ewe te çêdikir ew fênî ewe ew... cebar bî
jin... karê dijwar bû?
 
We saw that, you women used to fix them... female
bonesetters... was it a difficult job?

496
00:32:56,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Welle ew ê kar we dijwar... min tu fêr me ez ji vana yê wî
me tu hîn bû... we tiştek hûr u dît min çêdikiri ew e.
 
By God, the work was difficult... I learned from them... I
saw small things and I fixed them, that's it.

497
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:08,000
Ev ê wisa em qicikan wê datînin wê... ev qicik e...
 
Like this we place the small sprains there... this is a
small one...

498
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Ew çi ye ev tu pê dikî... ew?
 
What is this that you use... that?

499
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Ewe qicik we derdikeve we bîzmeca ye... u em... de.
 
That is a small dislocation, a bizmeca... and we... yes.

500
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Em bi bîzmeca fênî didin u te ew bi nav u tu wê fênî
dişidînin u qayiş u... tişt?
 
We give bizmeca, and you use that name and tighten it and a
strap and... things?

501
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:25,000
Ev an nav bi tirkî tu te ev an we kurmancî ye, ev çiye?
 
Is this name in Turkish or is it in Kurmanji, what is this?

502
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Welle ez nizanim tirkî ye an bi kurmancî ye ev bîzmeca yê
ewe...
 
By God I don't know if it's Turkish or Kurmanji, this is a
bizmeca...

503
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:32,000
Ewe qicikek e şkestî ye u em u wê didin hev u ew tu u tu we
pê nû we u sax dibe.
 
It's a small broken bone and we put it together and you use
it and it gets well again.

504
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Ka cî sabûn tu we u hêk me... we di me de bide naskirin ewe
nav te?
 
Tell us about the soap and the egg... introduce these to us?

505
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:40,000
Ev we sabûn e... am pê dişon.
 
This is soap... we wash with it.

506
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Ev hêk e... am spîka hêkê we diderînîn em jê de we cî.
 
This is an egg... we pour the egg white from it and use it.

507
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:49,000
U ev paç e fênî we u we te em pê...
 
And this is a bandage and we use it to...

508
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Ev we xwê tu we fênî u kelandin we me tu yê an te wê.
 
This is salt, we boil it and use it.

509
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:59,000
u me yê rûn ew yê pê dest wek datanîn wî de an u şkestîn tu
de me wisa me datanî.
 
And we use oil, put it on by hand into the fracture like
that, we place it.

510
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Ev...
 
This...

511
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Ev tu xwê di kelînin wê me we u xwê germ em wî di şkestî em
te wisa datînin wê.
 
This is salt, we boil it and hot salt we put into the
fracture like that.

512
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Tu destpêkê wî tiştek di wê şûnda te yek pê çêdikî?
 
Do you start by putting something in there, and then fix it?

513
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Ew we u germ wê xwê u wê u ez te paç... u şidandin wê me.
 
We put hot salt on it and then a bandage... and we tighten
it.

514
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Min me ew şûşt we bi destan me.
 
I wash it with my hands.

515
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:23,000
Me fêr ew yê derdixistin ew u jê dikişîne... tu te qata wê
nehişt te we ber.
 
I expertly pulled it out and stretch it... you didn't let
its place go.

516
00:34:23,000 --> 00:34:26,000
U we hêk wî kîjan wê u dem we yê u me de tu diderî?
 
And at what time do you put the egg in it?

517
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:35,000
Ba wê me yê heke nexweşî wê de ew em pîş wî me we yê de ew
de we spîka hêkê tu cî we nav diderînîn.
 
When the patient needs it, we put it on beforehand, we pour
the egg white on it.

518
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:54,000
u em de we wî nav wisa diderî ew u dî... we wî u di u me yê.
Em we nav wisa me u we u me ew de.
 
And we pour it inside like that... and that's it. We pour it
inside like that.

519
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Navên hin din hene te fêr tu cebar bikî tu çi diki navê wan?
 
Are there other names that you set bones for, what are their
names?

520
00:34:56,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Nabin ez nav dî te yek kes an cebar bikim kes an tişt şûna
wan... ez qey ez nas nakim ciyê.
 
There aren't, I can't name others that I set bones for, or
someone's place... I don't really know their places.

521
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Baş e siheta te xweş be dê tu baş em ê tu te nas dikin bi
vê.
 
Alright, may you be in good health mother, we know you well
through this.

522
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Spasiya te dikin.
 
We thank you.

523
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,000
A te jî xweş be bavo.
 
May you be as well, my son.

524
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Lê qey tu kesek dî hîn nekir bavo fêr bikî an yek... fênî tu
te wî... ?
 
But haven't you taught anyone else, my dear, someone else to
learn?

525
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Wele ew u bavê min ez te hîn we u ew cî kes qey tu yê hîn
nebû u.
 
By God, my father taught me, and nobody else really learned.

526
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Lê ez bi dest we cî me ew we wextê ew wî dişkestî u me fênî
de ez u de me datanî ew u we de ez.
 
But I used my hands when they had a broken bone, and I would
put it in place, and that's it.

527
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Baş e siheta te xweş be dê.
 
Alright, may you be in good health, mother.

528
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:30,000
A te jî xweş be u Xwedê razî be bavo.
 
May you be as well, and may God be pleased, my son.

529
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:32,000
Ê siheta te jî xweş be dê.
 
And may you be in good health too, mother.

530
00:35:32,000 --> 00:35:33,000
A te jî xweş be lawê min.
 
May you be as well, my son.

531
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Te jimir nedikir te ev çiye, ev an tişt te we derman?
 
You didn't count for us, what is this, these medicines?

532
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:40,000
Weleh we ew wî derman an de wek ez nizam bavo de ez ...
 
By God, those medicines, I don't know my son, I...

533
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Ez derman... nav we ber we nizanim ... wê tişt nizanim ez
te.
 
I don't know the names of the medicines... I don't know
those things.

534
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Ez ê we ew çê me an ew bî u ez di we de wî an me nav kêm ewe
wî yê.
 
I used to make them, but I forgot their names.

535
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:49,000
Navê te çiye dê?
 
What is your name, mother?

536
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Hewrik.
 
Hewrik.

537
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:52,000
Hewrik?
 
Hewrik?

538
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Hewrik êh.
 
Yes, Hewrik.

539
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:55,000
Siheta te xweş be Hewrik, bixêr hatî.
 
May you be in good health Hewrik, welcome.

540
00:35:55,000 --> 00:36:15,000
A te jî xweş be.
 
May you be as well.

541
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Gund bi navê xwe, çar pakrewan hene.
 
In the village by its name, there are four martyrs.

542
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Şehîd Mahîr, Rengîn, Arif û Şehîd Hemo.
 
Martyr Mahir, Rengin, Arif, and Martyr Hamo.

543
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Dibistana gund bi navê Şehîd Arif e û komîna gund jî bi navê
Şehîd Mahîr e, komîna jinan jî bi navê Şehîd Rengîn e.
 
The village school is named after Martyr Arif, and the
village commune is named after Martyr Mahir, and the women's
commune is named after Martyr Rengin.

544
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:37,000
Di dîwanxaneya yekemîn di gund de, ya Şêx Seydo bû.
 
In the first guest house in the village, it belonged to
Sheikh Seydo.

545
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Mêvanperweriya wî hembêz dikir bo hemî rêwiyan, u xelkê
derdorê yê weşand dikir şêx...
 
His hospitality embraced all the travelers, and the people
of the surroundings used to spread the word of the sheikh...

546
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Şêx Seydo nêzîkî çil salî mixtarê gund bû.
 
Sheikh Seydo was the headman of the village for nearly forty
years.

547
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:50,000
Hemîdê Hemo an u Xelîlê Seydî, Mistê Hesê û Kono ji rûspiyên
gund bûn.
 
Hemide Hemo, and Xelile Seydi, Miste Hese, and Kono were
among the village elders.

548
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Û wek her di gundekî wisa jî jinek jî bi navê Meyro
nexweşiyan çêdikir.
 
And as in every such village, a woman named Meyro would
treat illnesses.

549
00:36:55,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Nêzîkî pêncî kes ji gund an bawernameyên bilind wergirtine.
 
Nearly fifty people from the village have received higher
degrees.

550
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Ji wan, bijîjk, endazyar, mamoste û karmend an li dezgeh û
perwerdeyê xwedî kar cî girtin e.
 
Among them, doctors, engineers, teachers, and employees took
positions in institutions and education.

551
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Merheba ciwano.
 
Hello young men.

552
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:43,000
Silav.
 
Greetings.

553
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:45,000
Merheba hûn bixêr hatin serçavan.
 
Hello, welcome, you are dear to me.

554
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Em te nas bikin?
 
Can we know you?

555
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,000
Navê min Nîhad e.
 
My name is Nihad.

556
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Nîhad, u te?
 
Nihad, and you?

557
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:51,000
Navê min jî Riyad e.
 
My name is also Riyad.

558
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:54,000
Nîhad û Riyad... çi navên xweş in. Hûn li deştê... xwe hûn
cî bi mêşvaniyê dikin?
 
Nihad and Riyad... what lovely names. Are you in the
field... working with beekeeping?

559
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Ema we tu dibînî em nav çolê de em wî kar dikin.
 
Well, as you can see, we are doing this work out in the
wild.

560
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:00,000
Xweş kar e, u karê zehmet e... wisa pîşeya de.
 
It's a nice job, and a hard one... in this profession.

561
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:02,000
Pîşeyeke xweş e em bi fênî kar wisa tu dî dikin.
 
It's a nice profession, we are working well like this as you
see.

562
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Hûn xudanên mêşxudan in, herdu?
 
You are both beekeepers, right?

563
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,000
Belê em herdu.
 
Yes, both of us.

564
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Te sal tu, çi wext tu fêrî an u kar?
 
How many years, since when did you learn this work?

565
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Wele me ji bavkê xwe wî nav an di ew kar me girtî.
 
By God, we took this work from our father.

566
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:12,000
Te çend sal e ev di emrê te tu mêşxudanî an tu ev kar dikî?
 
How many years in your life have you been a beekeeper or
doing this work?

567
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:15,000
Welleh temenê me, teqrîben bîst û pênc an, sî û panzdeh,
bîst salî de em dizanin...
 
By God, our age, approximately twenty-five or thirty, since
fifteen, twenty years we've known...

568
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:20,000
Bavê min di kor de ew kar dikir, û min bavê xwe fêr u we hîn
bûm me mêş u de fêr.
 
My father did this work, and I learned and grew accustomed
to it from my father, learning about bees.

569
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:23,000
Cudahî an ferq navbera vana de çiye? Ew edetî u ê fênî.
 
What is the difference between these? The traditional one
and the modern (technical) one.

570
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:33,000
Na... ferqa nabera meşa fênî u wî mêşa an wî edetî... mêşa
wî berê bî em we me yê wekî mîrat bû...
 
Well... the difference between the modern hive and the
traditional one... the bees in the past, it was like a
heritage for us...

571
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:41,000
Ew fênî we u we tu fênî u ciyê an intaca wî zêde tu... dide,
tu pê fênî we wisa serederiyê u hêsantir e.
 
The modern one gives more production, and it is easier to
manage and work with.

572
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Wê hingiv u intaca wan zêdetir e fênî.
 
Their honey and production is much higher in the modern
ones.

573
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:52,000
Ê de ewana me an fênî mêşan bêtir em terxî we u kar dikin.
 
And so we dedicate our work more to the modern beehives.

574
00:38:52,000 --> 00:38:54,000
Tu piranî edetî u fênî tu... bi kîjan we kar bêtir dikî?
 
Do you mostly work with the traditional or the modern
ones... which one more?

575
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,000
Piranî fênî we.
 
Mostly the modern ones.

576
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Wê intaca wan an meş u çiqas digre navbera an fênî?
 
How much is their production, how much does the modern hive
hold?

577
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Ew meşa edetî yê bî we u an me sê u pênc kîlo dida bes ewana
fênî u tu 10 kîlo 15, 20 kîlo bî wê u dide.
 
The traditional hive used to give us three or five kilos,
but this modern one gives 10, 15, or 20 kilos.

578
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:09,000
Gelek u bide, hûn u mêşê xwe cî tu çolê u cî... hûn dibin
kuderê meşan diçêrînin?
 
If it gives a lot, where do you take your bees to the
field... where do you graze the bees?

579
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Welle an mentîqên wezîfa an... sûriye wî me cî u u de.
 
By God, in the regions of... Syria, we would go.

580
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Ji ber ku an mantîqa meşe te tu bî teng bû wî diçe
Laziqiyê... de em dibirin an Humsê te an.
 
Because if the bee area became narrow, they go to Latakia...
we used to take them there or to Homs.

581
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:25,000
Ewe me dûr we u sînor der digerand, niha me u we wî u rewşa
li Sûriyê ji ber wî an em Sûrke... ew Sûrke u şediyan we em
der dikin...
 
We used to roam far and outside the borders, now because of
the situation in Syria, we take them to Surke... to Surke
and those shaded areas...

582
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:29,000
Em dibin wê wî fênî cî der u aliciya an u we xwaşêle we.
 
We take them there, towards the Alici side and to the
Khwashele plants.

583
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:31,000
Wê ciya te aliciya an xwaşêle ew?
 
That place, Aliciya or Khwashele?

584
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Xwaşêle.
 
Khwashele.

585
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:34,000
Û li Humsê u we çi hebû wê?
 
And in Homs, what was there?

586
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:36,000
Li Humsê an we yanisûn u heye.
 
In Homs, there is anise.

587
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:37,000
Yanisûn e, u li Laziqiyê?
 
Anise, and in Latakia?

588
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:39,000
Li Laziqiye jî, an wî wek hemdiyat e.
 
In Latakia as well, there are citrus fruits.

589
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:47,000
U zivistanê wê wexta wî em bî ne dima we ji serma ne dima...
de em wê we u cî u tu we qişla dikir we ew hemdiyat...
 
And in winter time, we didn't stay, they wouldn't survive
the cold... so we would take them there to overwinter among
the citrus...

590
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:50,000
Gerek wî an we cî germ be?
 
Does it need to be a warm place?

591
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:55,000
Belî dê u wê wextê em an dibirin Lazqiyê... wî we cî u tu
germ wî dima.
 
Yes, at that time we took them to Latakia... so they would
stay in a warm place.

592
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,000
Tu mehan kîjan we wî destpê dikî u bî kar u mêş?
 
In which months do you start this bee work?

593
00:39:57,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Wextê we mehan bihar de an wî de em dest pê tu wî u dikin.
 
In the spring months, we start doing it.

594
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,000
Nû ve hûn pê re eleqedar in kengî?
 
Have you recently been interested in this, since when?

595
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Çêkirina van, berê hebûn yan na?
 
Making these, were they around before or not?

596
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Na, ev bav û kalê me heta niha, em van hingiva heta niha
xwedî dikin.
 
No, our ancestors until now, we have been keeping these bees
until now.

597
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:15,000
Ez hatim cem wan, min li xebatên wan temaşe kir, min jî
meraq kir wekî bav û kalên me vê senetê dikin.
 
I came to them, I watched their work, I was also curious
since our ancestors do this craft.

598
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Yanî bav û kalên te jî hingiv, yanî mêşvanî dikir?
 
So your ancestors also kept honey, I mean did beekeeping?

599
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:19,000
Rast e, rast e.
 
True, true.

600
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,000
Baş e.
 
Okay.

601
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:22,000
Çiqas qendîlên te hene?
 
How many hives do you have?

602
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,000
Welle em me yên fenni...
 
Well, our modern ones...

603
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Nêzîkî bîst qendîlan e.
 
Are around twenty hives.

604
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,000
Bîst qendîlên me yên fenni li vira ne.
 
We have twenty modern hives here.

605
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Û yên edî jî...
 
And the traditional ones too...

606
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:34,000
Bîst adî ne, bîst fenni ne.
 
Twenty are traditional, twenty are modern.

607
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,000
Ên din jî çiqas in?
 
How many are the others?

608
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,000
Ên din jî...
 
The others too...

609
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,000
Sîh adî ne...
 
Thirty are traditional...

610
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:43,000
Û çil jî adî ne.
 
And forty are also traditional.

611
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,000
Naha niha...
 
Now, currently...

612
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,000
Belê...
 
Yes...

613
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:48,000
Naha we dest pê kiriye, tiştekî din?
 
Now you have started, anything else?

614
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,000
Na na.
 
No no.

615
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:51,000
Mevsim xilas bûye.
 
The season has ended.

616
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:55,000
Ji ber me ew rakirin Xoşeliyê, em wan tînin, li vê derê em.
 
Because we took them to Xoşelyê, we bring them, here we.

617
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:59,000
Li vê derê em, wexta ku havinê, ji ber ku ev der hinek germ
e, hişk e, ciyê der e...
 
Here we, during the summer, because this place is a bit hot,
dry, it's a place...

618
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:02,000
Di zivistanê de çi dikin? Hûn wekî sermayê tiştekî li wan
dipêçin?
 
What do you do in the winter? Do you wrap something around
them for the cold?

619
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:04,000
Ev havanên we, tiştên din hûn li wan dipêçin an na?
 
These hives of yours, do you wrap other things around them
or not?

620
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:11,000
Na, me ev din, me rakirin ber çiyayê, ji ber ku ber çiyayê
germayiya wê ji vir zêdetir e, zivistanê.
 
No, these others, we took them to the foot of the mountain,
because the heat at the foot of the mountain is more than
here, in the winter.

621
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:14,000
Me rakirin wê derê û me danîn...
 
We took them there and placed them...

622
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,000
Yanî nêzîkî gundê we ye?
 
So it's near your village?

623
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Li pêş gund, kelekê gundê me ye. Ber çiyayê, hawarî de me
danîne wê derê.
 
In front of the village, beside our village. At the foot of
the mountain, in the valley we placed them there.

624
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Li wê derê jî zivistanê, em...
 
And there in the winter, we...

625
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:27,000
Wan jî û yên vê derê em hemî gişkan li hev dipêçin.
 
Those and the ones here we wrap them all up.

626
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Da ku serma û qeşa û berf zêde pê tesîr neke.
 
So that the cold and frost and snow don't affect them much.

627
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:32,000
Haziriyê bo biharê em ji wan re bikin.
 
We will make preparations for spring for them.

628
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,000
Baş e.
 
Okay.

629
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:38,000
Naha cam a te, hingivê nav cam a te çiye?
 
Now your jar, what is the honey in your jar?

630
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Hingivê nav camê anabê ye.
 
The honey in the jar is jujube.

631
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:56,000
Yê Xoşeliyê ye.
 
It's from Xoşelyê.

632
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:59,000
Na hingivê înnabê yê di cam de heye.
 
No, there is jujube honey in the jar.

633
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:01,000
Yê Xoşeliyê ye.
 
It's from Xoşelyê.

634
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:04,000
Hingivê biharê ye.
 
It's spring honey.

635
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:08,000
Vî, dema ko lazım dibe em xwarina melîk jê re dikin.
 
This, when it's needed we make queen food for it.

636
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Çawa çêdikin hûn wî?
 
How do you make that?

637
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Ewe ji qendîlê, ji qendîlê fennî em dertixin, giza melîk.
 
That's from the hive, from the modern hive we extract it,
queen food.

638
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:18,000
Ew jî bi graman derdikeve, hinekî zehmetiya wê heye, pir.
 
That also comes out in grams, it has some difficulty, a lot.

639
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:21,000
Ji ber wê...
 
Because of that...

640
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Mesela her însanek dixwaze, mesela dibêje giza melîk ji min
re amade bike.
 
For example, every person wants it, for example they say
prepare queen food for me.

641
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:28,000
Deh gram in, em di nav qutiyên biçûk de têxin, deh gram in.
 
It's ten grams, we put it in small boxes, it's ten grams.

642
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:30,000
Naha ew bîst gramê, teva kîloyekê dikin.
 
Now those twenty grams, they put into one kilo.

643
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:33,000
Yan jî dehî teva dikin.
 
Or they put ten in it.

644
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:37,000
Bi vî tonî hûn ew karê we meşîn in naha?
 
With this tone are you carrying out your work now?

645
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:40,000
Naha hingivê îsal bi çiqasê tê firotin?
 
Now, how much is this year's honey sold for?

646
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:43,000
Welleh, hingiv yê înnabê...
 
Well, the jujube honey...

647
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Bi nehtî, em didin.
 
We give it for ninety.

648
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,000
Yê Xoşeliyê bi heştêye.
 
The Xoşelyê one is for eighty.

649
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:50,000
Îsal gelekî biha ye yanî.
 
This year it's very expensive then.

650
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Hingiv biha ye loma jî, ji ber ku îsal hingiv kêm e.
 
Honey is expensive therefore, because this year honey is
scarce.

651
00:42:54,000 --> 00:42:58,000
Naha te kanî çi amadehiyan dikî? Em ji çi re amadebikin em
bi wêneyan bikin.
 
Now what preparations are you making? What should we prepare
for, let's take pictures.

652
00:42:58,000 --> 00:43:02,000
Niha ji ber karê mêşan pir nemaye, em dikin şima çêkin.
 
Now because not much bee work is left, we are going to make
wax.

653
00:43:02,000 --> 00:43:07,000
Çunke şimayên me hene em hazirî dikin ji bo biharê.
 
Because we have wax we make preparations for spring.

654
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:09,000
Vê yekê hûn ji çi çêdikin?
 
What do you make this from?

655
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:11,000
Ji şimayê bes em dihelînin...
 
From wax, but we melt it...

656
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,000
Hûn dîsa vedigerînin.
 
You reuse it again.

657
00:43:13,000 --> 00:43:14,000
Em dîsa vedigerînin.
 
We reuse it again.

658
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:16,000
Ka kuderê derdixin?
 
Where do you extract it?

659
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:19,000
Welle niha li hewşê em amade dikin, şima amade dikin.
 
Well now we are preparing it in the courtyard, preparing
wax.

660
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,000
Mala te?
 
Your house?

661
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:21,000
Ê kerem ke.
 
Yes, please.

662
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:41,000
Em biçin mala te jî.
 
Let's go to your house too.

663
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:48,000
Belê naha jî em ê binêrin çawa birêz Nihad, ew şimayê amade
dike.
 
Yes, now we will see how Mr. Nihad prepares that wax.

664
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Naha tu çawa dest pê dikî?
 
Now, how do you start?

665
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:52,000
Hawa şima ye...
 
Look, it's wax...

666
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:56,000
Em ê wî şimayî têkin ava germ.
 
We will put this wax in hot water.

667
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Ev ya salên çûyî ye?
 
This is from past years?

668
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:00,000
Ev a sala çûyî ye.
 
This is from the past year.

669
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:02,000
Em têkin ava germ, naha ev dixe de dihele.
 
We put it in hot water, now it melts in it.

670
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:04,000
Piştî wê di ava xwe de têkel dibe.
 
After that it mixes in its water.

671
00:44:04,000 --> 00:44:24,000
Belê kerem ke.
 
Yes, please go ahead.

672
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Yanî ev şima hazir nîne?
 
So this wax is not ready?

673
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:32,000
Hazir jî heye...
 
There is ready-made too...

674
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:37,000
Lê em wekî zêdetir ji bo mesrefa wê... em dikarin xwe
bigrin, pir biha dikeve ser me.
 
But we like mostly for its expense... we can manage
ourselves, it costs us too much.

675
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:40,000
Em pir şimayên xwe çêdikin.
 
We make a lot of our own wax.

676
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:42,000
Naha wekî em dihelînin...
 
Now as we melt it...

677
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:44,000
Çiqas dimîne gerkî xwe hetanî çêbe?
 
How long does it take until it is done?

678
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:47,000
Wellehî wekî rubê saetekê...
 
Well, like a quarter of an hour...

679
00:44:47,000 --> 00:44:49,000
Yanî panzdeh deqeyî çêdibe.
 
So it gets done in fifteen minutes.

680
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:51,000
Piştî wê, hûn çawa çêdikin?
 
After that, how do you make it?

681
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Em wê dûr kin...
 
We will pour it...

682
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:58,000
Em di dûyî de didin, têkin van aliyan...
 
We pour it in the other, put it in these sides...

683
00:44:58,000 --> 00:45:00,000
Mezin dibe hinek.
 
It gets a bit bigger.

684
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,000
Têxin ava sar, ava sar.
 
Put it in cold water, cold water.

685
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:03,000
Em ê bi şima.
 
We'll make it wax.

686
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,000
Dûv re çawa?
 
Then how?

687
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:05,000
Em qalib dikin, qalibên wî dikin?
 
Do we mold it, make its molds?

688
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Qalibên we hene?
 
Do you have molds?

689
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:08,000
Na çi çêbû paşî em ê ji vê derê...
 
No, whatever is done, then we from here...

690
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:11,000
Em qalib dikin di wan firaqan de.
 
We mold it in those containers.

691
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:14,000
Ji vir em wekî qalibekî derdixin em rêtikin me'melê.
 
From here we extract it as a mold, we pour it to the
factory.

692
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:16,000
Em rêtikin ma'melê, ku derê?
 
We pour it to the factory, where?

693
00:45:16,000 --> 00:45:20,000
Bajarê Ezezê heye... em rêtikin Ezezê.
 
There is one in the city of Azaz... we send it to Azaz.

694
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:24,000
Cem Cibrîl yê Ezezê heye, li Ezezê, cem wî.
 
We have Jibril from Azaz, in Azaz, at his place.

695
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:26,000
Niha hûn rêtikin ya na?
 
Now do you send it or not?

696
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:28,000
Erê em rêdikin biharê şima rêdikin.
 
Yes, we send it, we send the wax in the spring.

697
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:29,000
Biharê.
 
In the spring.

698
00:45:29,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Yanî hûn gava xwe qalib dikin...
 
So when you mold it yourselves...

699
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:34,000
Na em li vira... heta haziriya xwe dikin.
 
No, we here... until we make our preparation.

700
00:45:34,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Em dişînin me'melê, ew ji me re diqalibîne.
 
We send it to the factory, he molds it for us.

701
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,000
Qalib çêdike.
 
He makes the mold.

702
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:41,000
Çêdike û camên me hene... em naha hazir in.
 
He makes it and we have our jars... we are ready now.

703
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:48,000
Ka kerekê nîşanî me bide?
 
Let's see it once?

704
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:51,000
Wa te dît wexta we karek kir kî tê?
 
Look, you saw, when you did a job, who comes?

705
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:54,000
Em caran yeka re dixebitin... gava wê heye.
 
We sometimes work together... when it is available.

706
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:58,000
Wextê hingiv em bi hev re derdixin...
 
During honey time, we extract it together...

707
00:45:58,000 --> 00:46:01,000
Wextê ku di buharê de, wextê em...
 
During spring, when we...

708
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:09,000
Tiştekî çêdikin ji melîkan, yan tiştekî xirab dibe em hevdu
agahdar dikin, yan çi karekî meşan yê bi hev re heye em gişk
hevdû re dibin alîkar.
 
Make something from queens, or if something goes bad we
inform each other, or whatever bee work we have together, we
all help each other.

709
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:16,000
Ji ber ku tekkes... nema dikare karekî xwe bike, ev karê
meşan tenê nabe.
 
Because one person... can no longer do their work, this bee
work cannot be done alone.

710
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Gelekî bi zehmet e...
 
It's very difficult...

711
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:29,000
Yek bi tenê karek bike zehmet e, wexta meşe digre û em pê re
dixebitin bi hev re çêdibe, weha tenê mirov nikare.
 
It's hard for one person to do a job alone, when catching a
swarm and we work with it together it gets done, otherwise a
person cannot do it alone.

712
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:33,000
Niha em dişînin me'melê em wisa amade dikin bişînin, ew jî
weha amade difroşin me.
 
Now we send it to the factory, we prepare it like this to
send, and they sell it back to us ready like this.

713
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:35,000
Em bi vî avayî çêdikin.
 
We make it in this way.

714
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:37,000
Ha ew ê vedigerîne?
 
Ah, they return it?

715
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:40,000
Wek van şeklan vedigerîne.
 
They return it in these shapes.

716
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Niha de, li Efrînê kesên ku têne nas kirin, dibêjin di warê
meşandina meşan de karê wek kê ye?
 
Now, in Afrin, the people who are known, who do they say is
like someone in the field of beekeeping?

717
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:53,000
Welle piranî ne ji berê ve, hevalekî me yê navdar heye Ûsiv
Alewî yê ji gundê Omera,
 
Well, there are many from before, we have a famous friend
Yusuf Alawi from the village of Omera,

718
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Gundê Omera?
 
Village of Omera?

719
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:58,000
Gundê Omera ye ew jî dostê me ye hevalê me ye, ew jî karê
meşavaniyê dike.
 
The village of Omera, he is also our friend, our companion,
he also does beekeeping work.

720
00:46:58,000 --> 00:47:00,000
Wekî din kê?
 
Who else?

721
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:03,000
Ên din jî hene li herêma Cindirêsê jî hene,
 
There are others too in the Jindires region,

722
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:05,000
Yanî gelek kes hene?
 
So there are many people?

723
00:47:05,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Erê, erê hene.
 
Yes, yes there are.

724
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:08,000
Çiqas wext e... gundê Miskê jî yek hebû, wisa nîne?
 
For how long... there was someone in the village of Miske
too, isn't that so?

725
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:10,000
Erê hebû bes ema...
 
Yes there was, but...

726
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:13,000
Di wextê niha de pir meş kêm bûne da xebitînê.
 
At the current time, bees have decreased a lot to work with.

727
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:16,000
Pir bi zihmet ketiye karkirina wê de.
 
It has become very difficult in its working.

728
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:23,000
Û bi rastî ev karê meşên fenni, tu mijûlî van karî yî,
zêdeyî bîst salî bêtir e te dest bi vî karî kiriye, tu
mijûlî wê yî?
 
And truthfully this modern bee work, you are busy with this
work, it's been more than twenty years since you started
this work, you are busy with it?

729
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:43,000
Baş e em wê demê pêvajoyê bişopînin, ev niha bihele, pazdeh
deqe xwest.
 
Okay then let's follow the process, this needs to melt now,
it requires fifteen minutes.

730
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:49,000
Naha piştî ev di nava ava wê de tê çi dikin?
 
Now after this comes into its water, what do you do?

731
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:51,000
Piştî wê em...
 
After that we...

732
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:54,000
Şimaya we çêdibe em dihelînin da diqelînin em wek safî bikin
di nav ava germ de.
 
Your wax gets done, we melt it, we fry it to clarify it in
the hot water.

733
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:58,000
Piştre em dikin diqalibekê da wek vî qalibê we yê amade ye
em têkin qalib, wek we xistî em têxin firaxê de.
 
Then we put it in a mold like this mold of yours that is
ready, we put it in the mold, as you put it, we put it in
the container.

734
00:47:58,000 --> 00:48:02,000
Dûv re ev qalib e, em rêdikin ma'melê jê re amade derdixe.
 
Then this is the mold, we send it to the factory, it gets
prepared for it.

735
00:48:02,000 --> 00:48:04,000
Ev e jî hazirtî derket ji me re...
 
This preparation came out ready for us...

736
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:08,000
Bi buharê em ê dest bi karkirina wê bikin em bişînin wê
derê, hingiv dê derkeve, naha...
 
In spring we will start its work, we will send it there,
honey will come out, now...

737
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Yanî hun zivistanê çi xizmetên wan nakin tu nikarî zivistanê
destê xwe têxî wan?
 
So you don't do any service for them in winter, you can't
put your hand in them in winter?

738
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,000
Na em zivistanê qet karek nînin wan weha dimînin.
 
No, we don't have any work in winter, they stay like that.

739
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:16,000
Xizmeta wê tiştek tine ye?
 
Is there no service for it?

740
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:17,000
Qet xizmeta wê weha tineye.
 
There is no service for it like that at all.

741
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:18,000
Tu şurûbek tu tiştek, derman nadî?
 
You don't give any syrup, anything, medicine?

742
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:20,000
Na... dermanê wî tiştek wisa tineye bi zivistanê de...
 
No... there is no medicine or anything like that in
winter...

743
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:22,000
Dest pê dike ew kar di biharê de...
 
That work begins in the spring...

744
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:25,000
Dest bi dermanan bikin yan nexweşiyê bigirin wek em
bişopînin di biharê de, wisa de.
 
Start the medicines or catch diseases as we follow in
spring, like that.

745
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:27,000
Di tiştê ku zivistanê diqedînin, û nexweşî tune bibe...
 
In the thing that finishes in winter, and the disease
disappears...

746
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:28,000
Hingiv zêde derxînin.
 
They produce more honey.

747
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:33,000
Naha carekê ev bi rastî ev di mêjiyê min de çêdibû ez
dixwazim ji te bipirsim;
 
Now once this really happened in my mind, I want to ask you;

748
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:35,000
Em dibêjin ev hingivê sax e ev yê ne sax e, çi yê ne sax e?
 
We say this honey is pure, this one is not pure, what is the
not pure one?

749
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:40,000
Ma ew şekir çêdikin çi tê de zêde dikin, hûn dikarin hinekê
li ser wê yekê mijarê biaxifîn?
 
Do they make sugar, what do they add to it, can you talk a
bit about this topic?

750
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:42,000
Wellehî hingivê sax, yê normal...
 
Well, pure honey, normal one...

751
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:45,000
Hingiv bi xwe, te bi xwe di çolê de girtiyê amade ye.
 
The honey itself, you caught it yourself in the wild, ready.

752
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:48,000
Yê ku tê amadekirin bêyî şekir yê xwezayî ye...
 
The one that is prepared without sugar is the natural one...

753
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:52,000
Hinek şekir pir didinê, şekir dikelînin nava avê de û didin
meşê ev ya nexweş e ya bi şekir derdikeve.
 
Some give a lot of sugar, they boil sugar in water and give
it to the bees, this is the bad one that comes out with
sugar.

754
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:54,000
Yanî şekir didin meşê an ew bi xwe çêdikin, çawa ye?
 
So they give sugar to the bees or they make it themselves,
how is it?

755
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:55,000
Erê ewe didin.
 
Yes, they give that.

756
00:48:55,000 --> 00:48:58,000
Dihelînin dikin nav avê û didin meşan ev nexweş e...
 
They melt it, put it in water and give it to the bees, this
is unhealthy...

757
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:00,000
Lê em bi van tiştan tevnagerin, van tiştan nadin wan.
 
But we do not engage with these things, we do not give these
things to them.

758
00:49:00,000 --> 00:49:05,000
Me pêdivî bi hingivê xwezayî saxlem e ji bo saxlemiyê em
dixwazin bila paqij be derkeve.
 
We need healthy natural honey, for health we want it to come
out pure.

759
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:08,000
Yanî yê saxlem ew bi tenê hingivê normal e yê xwezayî ye.
 
So the healthy one is only the normal natural honey.

760
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:12,000
Yanî yê normal yê saxlem e ku, wek bi giştî tê zanîn di nav
xelkê de bê şekir bibe yê saxlem e?
 
So the normal pure one is, as it is generally known among
the people, if it is without sugar it is pure?

761
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Ma yanî em şekir nadin wan heta hûn nizanin wan jî didin
wan,
 
Do you mean we don't give sugar to them, even you don't know
they also give it to them,

762
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:16,000
Ên din didinê, lê em nadin, yanî yê normal ew e ku yê tu
şekir tê de tuneye.
 
The others give it, but we don't, I mean the normal one is
the one with no sugar in it.

763
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:18,000
Meş xwe amade hingiv berhev dike.
 
The bee gathers honey ready by itself.

764
00:49:18,000 --> 00:49:20,000
Lê kêm berhev dike dema ku hingiv normal be ne yê şekir be..
 
But it gathers less when the honey is normal, not the sugar
one.

765
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:21,000
Ne wek hingivê bi şekir pir dide..
 
Not like honey with sugar which gives a lot..

766
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:25,000
Yanî yê xwezayî ye, hun wek çêdikin hingivê te paqij û
xwezayî ye. Wek tu dibêjî ewe,
 
So it's natural, like you make it, your honey is pure and
natural. As you say that is,

767
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:26,000
Belê wisa ye.
 
Yes, it is like that.

768
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:28,000
Kar û xebata te ya vî, çiqas jê hez dikî tu ji vê hez dikî?
 
Your work and labor of this, how much do you like it, do you
like this?

769
00:49:28,000 --> 00:49:32,000
Welleh ev kar xweş e lê.. xebata we hinek zemet e, pir zemet
e..
 
Well, this work is nice but.. your labor is a bit hard, very
